It is important to be honest when lying on your resume, as it can damage your credibility and make you vulnerable to getting caught. Here are some things you could consider lying about on your resume:

- Lying about the name of the company you worked for;
- Lying about the responsibilities you had in a certain job;
- Lying about the date you started or left a company;
- Lying about your level of education;
- Lying about the name of software you used if it was not the specific one mentioned;
- Lying about the amount of money you earned.
